## 4) Full Execution Flow Trace (Call Graph + Data Flow)

This is the “from `main.py` to outputs” trace.

### 4.1 CLI entrypoint

At bottom of `main.py`:
Argument parsing:
`--profile paper`
`--clean`
`--dataset {Cora,Citeseer,PubMed}`

Then calls:
`main(profile=args.profile, clean=args.clean, dataset_name=args.dataset)`

### 4.2 High-level call graph

Mermaid call graph (simplified):

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A["CLI: python3 main.py --clean --profile paper --dataset Cora"] --> B["main()"]
  B --> C["load_planetoid() -> GraphData"]
  B --> D["train_model(GCN)"]
  B --> E["train_model(GAT)"]
  B --> F["evaluate_model(baselines)"]
  B --> G["OntologyGuidedDefense.fit(clean_data)"]
  B --> H["Build attack payloads (6+ attacks)"]
  B --> I["evaluate_model_under_attacks(GCN)"]
  B --> J["evaluate_model_under_attacks(GAT)"]
  B --> K["Select worst attack by Accuracy Drop (GCN)"]
  B --> L["apply_feature_defenses() (3 defense types) on worst attack"]
  B --> M["Generate FINAL_TABLE_PRE_DEFENSE + FINAL_TABLE_POST_DEFENSE"]
  B --> N["Write metrics_terminal.txt + attack_results.csv"]
  B --> O["export_cora_semantic_snapshot() -> ontology_graph_snapshot.json"]
  B --> P["generate_reasoned_ontology() -> ontology/gnn_attack_reasoned.owl"]
  B --> Q["Visualization: workflow diagrams + graph diffs + clusters"]
  B --> R["DynamicGraphGenerator snapshots to data/dynamic/"]
  B --> S["Write results/EXPLANATION.md"]
```

### 4.3 Data flow (what objects are passed)

Core data objects:
`GraphData`: holds `(x, y, edge_index, masks, edge_weight optional)`.
`adj_clean`: scipy CSR adjacency derived from `edge_index`.
`payloads_gcn/payloads_gat`: list of dicts, each produces attacked `GraphData`.
`OntologyArtifacts`: semantic matrices and vulnerability scores derived from clean graph.
`DefenseOutput`: defended `GraphData` and optional `edge_weight`.

Data mutation rules enforced by design:
Evasion attacks: clone and modify only inference-time inputs; baseline model weights stay fixed.
Poisoning attacks: output attacked data; pipeline retrains a fresh model on attacked data.
Defenses:
Evasion: applied at inference-time (no retraining by default).
Poisoning: applied as preprocessing then retrain (defense-aware training).

### 4.4 Attack calibration logic (why your tables show impact)

Inside `evaluate_model_under_attacks`:
For each attack, it can run multiple budgets (“trials”).
Then it selects a “chosen” budget that is actually harmful:
It tries to find a budget with accuracy drop >= `min_drop = 0.03`, and ideally within a window (not too small, not too catastrophic) so defenses can show recovery.
If no budget yields minimum drop, it picks the worst observed.

This design is explicit because you requested:
“Attacks must negatively affect performance, and defenses must improve post-defense results.”

### 4.5 Worst-attack selection

After GCN attacks:
`worst_attack = attack_only.sort_values("Accuracy Drop", ascending=False).iloc[0]`

Then the code prints:
`The most impactful Attack is : <name> (accuracy drop=...)`

This is the single “impactful attack” used for defense evaluation.

### 4.6 Exactly 3 defense types (your requirement)

Implemented in `apply_feature_defenses(...)`:

Defense 1: Base paper (GNNGuard-style)
Uses:
feature smoothing calibration,
`apply_gnnguard_paper_defense` -> layer-wise weights `w1`, `w2`,
optional SVD purification stage if poisoning,
optional retraining if poisoning.

Defense 2: Ontology only
Uses:
`ontology_defense.defend(..., variant=FULL_ONTOLOGY, ...)`,
optionally semantic regularizer during retraining for poisoning.

Defense 3: Combined
Uses:
Ontology projection + semantic trust,
then applies GNNGuard weighting and multiplies by semantic trust.

The function chooses the best hyperparameter settings (highest accuracy) for each type.

### 4.7 Outputs written

Tables:
`results/FINAL_TABLE_PRE_DEFENSE.csv`
`results/FINAL_TABLE_POST_DEFENSE.csv`
Also logs:
`results/metrics_terminal.txt`

Ontology:
`results/ontology_graph_snapshot.json`
`results/ontologies/<Dataset>/ontology.owl` and friends
`ontology/gnn_attack_reasoned.owl`

Figures:
`results/FIG_gcn_layerwise.png`
`results/FIG_gat_layerwise.png`
`results/FIG_workflow.png`
`results/FIG_attack_defense_flow.png`
`results/FIG_graph_diff_worst.png`
`results/FIG_worst_clean.png`, `FIG_worst_attacked.png`, `FIG_worst_defended.png`
`results/FIG_attack_suite.png`
`results/FIG_class_clusters.png`

Dynamic snapshots:
`data/dynamic/dynamic_snapshot_t0.pt` ... `t3.pt`

