## 8) Results: How To Read and Scientifically Interpret

Primary result outputs:
`results/FINAL_TABLE_PRE_DEFENSE.csv`
`results/FINAL_TABLE_POST_DEFENSE.csv`

Both tables include:
Model, Attack, Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1, Macro F1, Micro F1,
ROC-AUC, Log-loss, Classification Margin, Robustness Score,
Attack Success Rate (relative accuracy drop), Margin Drop,
Perturbation Rate, Perturbation Budget, Accuracy Drop.

Interpretation:
Accuracy Drop is the key severity metric used to select worst attack.
Macro F1 is important when classes are imbalanced.
ROC-AUC shows ranking quality, sometimes stable even when accuracy drops.
Log-loss increases when model becomes overconfident but wrong.
Margin drop indicates reduced separation between top classes.

Graph metrics:
`results/graph_metrics_static.csv` compares clean vs attacked vs defended:
Density, modularity, conductance, homophily, avg degree, number of edges.

Scientific explanation template (for IEEE/viva):
“Attack X reduces accuracy by Δ because it perturbs (A/X) causing message passing to aggregate off-topic signals, reducing homophily and increasing neighborhood entropy. Defense Y restores performance by pruning low-trust edges and projecting features back into a topic-consistent semantic subspace, improving homophily and modularity and reducing embedding drift.”

